[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! ## What "input" means for this program
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `c_src/src/main.c` declares `int main(void)` and never touches `stdin`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `argv`, the environment, the clock or the RNG (verified by grepping the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! source for `scanf`/`fgets`/`getchar`/`read`/`argv`/`argc`/`getenv`/`stdin`/
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `time`/`rand`/`clock`). It is a fixed test driver: the "input" it branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! is compiled in, and it is exercised in full on every run.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Two consequences drive the design of this file:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! 1. The internal branch classes (empty tree, single node, `MAX_CHILDREN`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!    saturation, duplicate id, hashmap resize/collision, subtree removal, root
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!    removal, path finding) are all reached by a single run. `landmarks`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!    asserts each one actually shows up in the observed output, so the suite
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!    fails loudly if a future edit stops exercising one of them rather than
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!    silently comparing less.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! 2. The axes that *can* vary between invocations are the process-level ones:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!    stdin contents, argv, environment, working directory, and how stdout and
